            <ArticleTitle>Endovascular stent-graft treatment of type A dissection: case report and review of literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>457-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a successful endovascular stent-graft treatment of a patient with type A dissection with primary entry tear at the ascending aorta. Simultaneous coronary stenting was performed. A literature review was performed and the possible use of endovascular treatment for ascending aortic dissections is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
